# More rational expressions where the first simplify result is not a fixed point.
# In each, s1 has a leading minus sign "-(...)/(...)"; s2 pushes it into the
# numerator and reorders the denominator, and s3 == s2.
simplify 2/x - 3/y
simplify -(3x - 2y)/(x*y)
simplify (2y - 3x)/(y*x)
simplify 1/x - 1/y - 1/z
simplify -(x*y + x*z - y*z)/(x*y*z)
simplify (y*z - y*x - z*x)/(y*z*x)
simplify 1/a - 1/b
simplify -(a - b)/(a*b)
simplify (b - a)/(b*a)
simplify x*(1/x - 1/y)
simplify -(x - y)/y
simplify (y - x)/y
